{
	title: 'SYSTEM.md preprocessor: comments, if blocks, variables, includes',
	spec: 'SYSTEM.md is preprocessed before it joins the system prompt (src/host/system-prompt.ts; AGENTS.md files and included files are not preprocessed, but lose their HTML comments too: nobody writes a comment by accident, so comments are notes for humans everywhere). In order: HTML comments <!-- ... --> are removed (multi-line too); "::: if key=\\"glob\\"" ... ":::" blocks keep their lines only when the variable matches the glob (* any run, ? one char, other punctuation literal; directive lines stand alone with three or more colons; several key="glob" pairs on one line must all match; no else, nesting or escaping; an unclosed block or unknown key is an error naming the line, shown to the user, not silently dropped); includes: a line that is only @path is replaced by that file\'s verbatim text (not preprocessed: no comments removed, conditions, variable substitution or nested includes; paths relative to SYSTEM.md, ~ expands) and fails loudly when missing, while @?path is replaced by the file if it exists and by nothing if it does not; included text starting with @ or ::: is ordinary text; then ${variable} placeholders are replaced: harness (hal), model (provider/id), date, cwd (~ shortened), hal_dir, home (the home root), session_dir, hal_source (true when cwd is inside the Hal checkout). Unknown ${...} stay as they are. The result must stay byte-identical for the same inputs (caching), so no variable may change mid-session except through the inputs that already reach the prompt (cwd, model). Artifact old-system-prompt.ts (reference: its header comment and conditional-block code). Tests: comments gone; an if block kept and dropped by model; two conditions; unclosed block error; @ include, @? present and absent, missing @ fails, included directives remain literal; variables replaced only in SYSTEM.md.',
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'Only SYSTEM.md is a template; AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md and includes remain literal except that HTML comments are stripped from every prompt file (user decision 28 Sep). Include paths resolve variables first (for @?${home}/USER.md), while unknown placeholders remain; session_dir is supplied from turns.ts.',
		'Included files are inserted raw and only SYSTEM.md itself is preprocessed; substituting after joining would still expand USER.md variables. Includes do not recurse, so a USER.md @ line cannot cause a failed request.',
		'Bug fix 8 Oct: a broken SYSTEM.md (unknown :::if key) failed every request in every session. Invariant restored: prompt files never fail or stall a turn. Faults (missing SYSTEM.md, unknown key, invalid/nested/unclosed/stray directive, missing @ include) are collected with file:line, the faulty part is dropped, the rest applies; turns.ts shows them once per session as a notice and again when they change. /system inspect returns them too.',
		'Variable user_notes: true unless HAL_NO_USER_NOTES is set; SYSTEM.md wraps the User notes section and the USER.md include in ::: if user_notes="true", so benchmarks run without the user\'s notes.',
		'Prompt files support ::: else inside an if block; else without if is reported as a problem.'
	],
	needs: ['tm']
}
